& =\frac{4}{9} \sum_{1 \leq i<j \leq 4} \frac{1}{a_{i}+a_{j}} \tag{1}
\end{align*}
$$

Let $a_{1}=a, a_{2}=b, a_{3}=c, a_{4}=d$.
We'll show that
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{2}{9}\left(\frac{1}{a+b}+\frac{1}{a+c}+\frac{1}{a+d}+\frac{1}{b+c}+\frac{1}{b+d}+\frac{1}{c+d}\right) \\
