From (1) and (2) we obtain the given inequality.

Equality holds when $a_1 = a_2 = a_3 = a_4$, that is, when the quadrilateral is equilateral. In this case, both sides of the inequality are equal, so the minimum value of $C$ for which the inequality always holds is $C = \frac{2}{9}$.

Therefore, the answer is $C = \frac{2}{9}$.

