Equality holds when $a = b = c = \frac{1}{3}$, which corresponds to $x = y = z = 1$ (i.e., $\alpha = \beta = \gamma = \frac{\pi}{3}$), and in this case $a^2 + b^2 + c^2 + 2\sqrt{3abc} = 3\left(\frac{1}{9}\right) + 2\sqrt{3}\left(\frac{1}{27}\right) = \frac{1}{3} + \frac{2}{9} = 1$. This gives the maximum value of the expression, so the minimal constant $C$ is $1$.

