and we are done.

Equality holds when $x = y$, since all the inequalities above become equalities in this case. Substituting $x = y$ into the original inequality gives $C(2x^9) = (2x^2)(2x^3)(2x^4) = 8x^9$, so $C = 4$ is the smallest constant for which the inequality always holds (minimum value of $C$).

Therefore, the answer is $C = 4$.

