For any real numbers $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n}$ and $b_{1}, b_{2}, \ldots, b_{n}$

$$
\begin{gathered}
\left(a_{1}^{2}+a_{2}^{2}+\ldots+a_{n}^{2}\right)\left(b_{1}^{2}+b_{2}^{2}+\ldots+b_{n}^{2}\right) \geq \\
\geq\left(a_{1} b_{1}+a_{2} b_{2}+\ldots+a_{n} b_{n}\right)^{2}
\end{gathered}
$$

with equality if and only if $a_{i}$ and $b_{i}$ are proportional, $i=1,2, \ldots, n$.

solution:
Applying $A M \geq G M$ we have
$$
\begin{equation*}
\frac{1}{b(a+b)}+\frac{1}{c(b+c)}+\frac{1}{a(c+a)} \geq 3 \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{a b c(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}} \tag{1}
\end{equation*}
$$
and
$$
\begin{equation*}
a+b+c \geq 3 \sqrt[3]{a b c}, \quad \text { i.e. } \quad \frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{a b c}} \geq \frac{3}{a+b+c} \tag{2}
\end{equation*}
$$

Furthermore
$$
a+b+c=\frac{1}{2}((a+b)+(b+c)+(c+a)) \geq \frac{3}{2} \sqrt[3]{(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}
$$
i.e.
$$
\begin{equation*}
\frac{1}{\sqrt[3]{(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}} \geq \frac{3}{2(a+b+c)} \tag{3}
\end{equation*}
$$

Combining (2), (3) and (1) we get
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{1}{b(a+b)}+\frac{1}{c(b+c)}+\frac{1}{a(c+a)} & \geq 3 \cdot \sqrt[3]{\frac{1}{a b c(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}} \\
& \geq 3 \cdot \frac{3}{a+b+c} \cdot \frac{3}{2(a+b+c)}=\frac{27}{2(a+b+c)^{2}}
\end{aligned}
$$

Equality in the above inequalities holds when $a = b = c$, that is, when all variables are equal. In this case, the minimum value of the left-hand side is achieved, so $C = \frac{27}{2}$ is the largest constant for which the inequality always holds.

Therefore, the answer is $C = \frac{27}{2}$.

