\end{equation*}
$$

From (2) and (3) we get
$$
a^{2}+b^{2}+\frac{1}{a^{2}}+\frac{b}{a} \geq \sqrt{3}
$$

Equality occurs iff $b+\frac{1}{2 a}=0$ and $a^{2}=\frac{3}{4 a^{2}}$, i.e. $a= \pm \sqrt[4]{\frac{3}{4}}$ and $b=\mp \frac{1}{2} \sqrt[4]{\frac{4}{3}}$. Therefore, the answer is (B) $\geq$.

By $A M \geq G M$ we get
