But using the Cauchy-Schwarz Inequality and the AM-GM Inequality, we deduce that

$$
\begin{aligned}
& \sum_{i=1}^{n} \sqrt{\frac{a_{1}+a_{2}+\ldots+a_{i-1}+a_{i+1}+\ldots+a_{n}}{a_{i}}} \geq \\
& \geq \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{\sqrt{a_{1}}+\sqrt{a_{2}}+\ldots+\sqrt{a_{i-1}}+\sqrt{a_{i+1}}+\ldots+\sqrt{a_{n}}}{\sqrt{n-1} \cdot \sqrt{a_{i}}}= \\
& =\sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{\sqrt{a_{i}}}{\sqrt{n-1}}\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{a_{1}}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{a_{2}}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{\sqrt{a_{i-1}}}+\frac{1}{\sqrt{a_{i+1}}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{\sqrt{a_{n}}}\right) \geq \\
& \geq \sum_{i=1}^{n} \frac{(n-1) \sqrt{n-1} \cdot \sqrt{a_{i}}}{\sqrt{a_{1}}+\sqrt{a_{2}}+\cdots+\sqrt{a_{i-1}}+\sqrt{a_{i+1}}+\cdots+\sqrt{a_{n}}} \geq \\
& \geq \sum_{i=1}^{n}(n-1) \sqrt{\frac{a_{i}}{a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{i-1}+a_{i+1}+\cdots+a_{n}}}
\end{aligned}
$$

and we are done. Therefore, the answer is (B) $\geq$.

theorems.Theorem:
For any real numbers $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n}$ and $b_{1}, b_{2}, \ldots, b_{n}$

$$
\begin{gathered}
\left(a_{1}^{2}+a_{2}^{2}+\ldots+a_{n}^{2}\right)\left(b_{1}^{2}+b_{2}^{2}+\ldots+b_{n}^{2}\right) \geq \\
\geq\left(a_{1} b_{1}+a_{2} b_{2}+\ldots+a_{n} b_{n}\right)^{2}
