solution:
After some algebraic calculations we get
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \frac{4+2(a+b+c)}{2+a+b+c+a b c} \geq \frac{3 \sqrt{3}}{\sqrt{3}+1} \\
& \quad \Leftrightarrow \quad 2(2+a+b+c)(\sqrt{3}+1) \geq 3 \sqrt{3}(2+a+b+c+a b c) \\
& \quad \Leftrightarrow \quad 2+(a+b+c) \geq \frac{3 \sqrt{3}}{2-\sqrt{3}} a b c
\end{aligned}
$$
i.e.
$$
\begin{equation*}
2+(a+b+c) \geq 3 \sqrt{3}(2+\sqrt{3}) a b c . \tag{1}
\end{equation*}
$$

Applying $A M \geq G M$ we obtain
$$
1=a b+b c+c a \geq 3 \sqrt[3]{(a b c)^{2}}
$$
i.e.
$$
\begin{equation*}
\frac{1}{3 \sqrt{3}} \geq a b c \tag{2}
\end{equation*}
$$

Also we have
$$
\begin{equation*}
a+b+c \geq \sqrt{3} \tag{3}
\end{equation*}
$$

Using (2) and (3) we get
$$
2+(a+b+c) \geq 2+\sqrt{3} \geq 3 \sqrt{3}(2+\sqrt{3}) a b c
$$
i.e. we have shown inequality (1), as desired.

Equality holds if and only if $a=b=c=1 / \sqrt{3}$. Therefore, the answer is (B) $\geq$.

Without loss of generality we may assume that $a_{1} \geq a_{2} \geq \cdots \geq a_{n}$.
Then
$$
\frac{1}{2-a_{1}} \geq \frac{1}{2-a_{2}} \geq \cdots \geq \frac{1}{2-a_{n}}
$$

Now by Chebishev's inequality we have
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \left(a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{n}\right)\left(\frac{1}{2-a_{1}}+\frac{1}{2-a_{2}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{2-a_{n}}\right) \\
& \quad \leq n\left(\frac{a_{1}}{2-a_{1}}+\frac{a_{2}}{2-a_{2}}+\cdots+\frac{a_{n}}{2-a_{n}}\right)
\end{aligned}
$$
hence
$$
\begin{aligned}
\frac{a_{1}}{2-a_{1}}+\frac{a_{2}}{2-a_{2}}+\cdots+\frac{a_{n}}{2-a_{n}} & \geq \frac{1}{n}\left(\frac{1}{2-a_{1}}+\frac{1}{2-a_{2}}+\cdots+\frac{1}{2-a_{n}}\right) \\
& \geq \frac{1}{n} \cdot \frac{n^{2}}{2 n-\left(a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{n}\right)}=\frac{n}{2 n-1}
