& =6 \frac{\sqrt[3]{\frac{\lg a \lg b \lg c}{\lg b} \frac{\lg a}{\lg }}}{\sqrt[3]{(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}}=\frac{6}{\sqrt[3]{(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}}
\end{aligned}
$$

$$
\geq 6 \frac{3}{(a+b)+(b+c)+(c+a)}=\frac{9}{a+b+c}
$$

Equality holds when $a = b = c$, since then all terms are equal and the AM-GM inequalities used above become equalities. In this case, the minimum value of the left-hand side is achieved, so $C = 9$ is the maximal constant for which the inequality always holds.

Therefore, the answer is $C = 9$.

