& f(x)=\ln (1+x)-\frac{2 x}{2+x} \\
& g(x)=\ln (1+x)-\frac{x}{\sqrt{1+x}}
\end{aligned}
\]

It is easy to verify that \( f(0)=g(0)=0 \) and \( g'(0) \leqslant 0 \leqslant f'(0) \), and the inequalities are strict for \( x \neq 0 \). Indeed,

\[
\begin{aligned}
