& g'(x)=\frac{1}{1+x}-\frac{2+x}{2(1+x)^{3 / 2}}=-\frac{(1-\sqrt{1+x})^{2}}{2(1+x)^{3 / 2}}
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus, \( f(x)>0 \) for \( x>0 \) and \( f(x)<0 \) for \( x<0 \). This leads to the inequality on the right-hand side. The inequality on the left-hand side is obtained similarly. Therefore, the answer is (A) $\leq$.

Proof: Let $f(x)=(x-a_{1})(x-a_{2}) \cdots(x-a_{n})$,
$$
b_{j}=\frac{i}{n} \quad(0 \leqslant i \leqslant n) .
$$

By the Lagrange interpolation polynomial,
$$
\begin{aligned}
f(x)= & f\left(b_{0}\right) \frac{\left(x-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(x-b_{n}\right)}{\left(b_{0}-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(b_{0}-b_{n}\right)} \\
& +\cdots+f\left(b_{n}\right) \frac{\left(x-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(x-b_{n-1}\right)}{\left(b_{n}-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(b_{n}-b_{n-1}\right)}
\end{aligned}
$$

Let $S=\max _{0 \leqslant x \leqslant 1}|f(x)|$, then
$$
\begin{aligned}
\max _{0 \leqslant x \leqslant 2}|f(x)| \leqslant & \left|f\left(b_{0}\right) \frac{\left(x-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(x-b_{n}\right)}{\left(b_{0}-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(b_{0}-b_{n}\right)}\right| \\
& +\cdots+\left|f\left(b_{n}\right) \frac{\left(x-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(x-b_{n-1}\right)}{\left(b_{n}-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(b_{n}-b_{n-1}\right)}\right| \\
\leqslant & {\left[\begin{array}{l}
\left|\frac{\left(2-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(2-b_{n}\right)}{\left(b_{0}-b_{1}\right) \cdots\left(b_{0}-b_{n}\right)}\right|+\cdots \\
+\left|\frac{\left(2-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(2-b_{n-1}\right)}{\left(b_{n}-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(b_{n}-b_{n-1}\right)}\right|
\end{array}\right] . }
\end{aligned}
$$

Since
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \left|\frac{\left(2-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(2-b_{i-1}\right)\left(2-b_{i+1} \cdots\left(2-b_{n}\right)\right.}{\left(b_{n}-b_{0}\right) \cdots\left(b_{i}-b_{i-1}\right)\left(b_{i}-b_{i+1}\right) \cdots\left(b_{i}-b_{n}\right)}\right| \\
= & \frac{2 n(2 n-1) \cdots n}{i!(n-i)!(2 n-i)},
\end{aligned}
$$

Therefore,
$$
\begin{array}{c}
\max _{0 \leqslant x \leqslant 2}|f(x)| \leqslant S \sum_{i=1}^{n} C_{2 n-1}^{i} C_{2 n-1}^{n-i} \\
<S\left(\sum_{i=0}^{n} C_{2 n}^{i}\right)\left(\sum_{i=0}^{n} C_{2 n-i}^{n-i}\right)<S 2^{2 n} 2^{2 n-1}<S(16)^{n}
\end{array}
$$

Taking $C=16$ is sufficient. Therefore, the answer is (A) $\leq$.

